Reference implementation with a self-contained fixture harness (compare it with your own version only after your unaided attempt is recorded):

```python
import tempfile
from pathlib import Path


def summarize_scores(path):
    result = {"scores": {}, "skipped": [], "missing": False}
    try:
        f = open(path, encoding="utf-8")
    except FileNotFoundError:
        result["missing"] = True
        return result
    with f:
        for lineno, line in enumerate(f, 1):
            line = line.strip()
            if not line:
                continue
            name, sep, raw = line.rpartition(",")
            try:
                score = int(raw)
            except ValueError:
                score = None
            if not sep or not name or score is None:
                result["skipped"].append(lineno)
                continue
            best = result["scores"].get(name)
            if best is None or score > best:
                result["scores"][name] = score
    return result


with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as tmp:
    base = Path(tmp)
    (base / "s1.txt").write_text("ana,7\nbo,9\nana,8\n", encoding="utf-8")
    (base / "s2.txt").write_text("ana,7\nbo,x9\ncy,5\n", encoding="utf-8")
    print(summarize_scores(base / "s1.txt"))
    print(summarize_scores(base / "s2.txt"))
    print(summarize_scores(base / "missing.txt"))
```

Expected output:

```text
{'scores': {'ana': 8, 'bo': 9}, 'skipped': [], 'missing': False}
{'scores': {'ana': 7, 'cy': 5}, 'skipped': [2], 'missing': False}
{'scores': {}, 'skipped': [], 'missing': True}
```

Why it is shaped this way: open() is the only call inside the FileNotFoundError handler, so only a missing file sets missing to True and other errors still surface. The with f: block closes the file on every path. int(raw) is the only call inside the ValueError handler; a row is skipped when it has no comma, an empty name, or a non-integer score, and its 1-based line number is recorded. The best score per name is kept by comparing with the stored value, so ana ends at 8.
